From: OpenDesk <opendesk@openharmony.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Mar 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] Lib/ctypes/util.py: skip ldconfig on HarmonyOS

HarmonyOS does not have /sbin/ldconfig. Calling
_findSoname_ldconfig() would invoke subprocess.Popen(['/sbin/ldconfig', '-p']),
which raises SubprocessError. This causes ctypes.util.find_library() to crash
instead of gracefully returning None.

Many third-party libraries call find_library() (cffi, trio, Django GIS,
Sphinx, etc.), so this crash blocks a significant portion of the Python
ecosystem on HarmonyOS.

Fix: return None early on HarmonyOS platform, so callers fall through to
their own fallback logic (e.g., trying CDLL("libxxx.so") directly).

---
 Lib/ctypes/util.py | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Lib/ctypes/util.py b/Lib/ctypes/util.py
--- a/Lib/ctypes/util.py
+++ b/Lib/ctypes/util.py
@@ -257,6 +257,9 @@ def find_library(name):
         def _findSoname_ldconfig(name):
+            # HarmonyOS: no /sbin/ldconfig, skip to avoid SubprocessError
+            if sys.platform.startswith(('ohos', 'harmonyos')):
+                return None
             import struct
